r row by 1 and reducing the number of rows by 2, the new formation has $ (r - 2)(m + 1) $ places, and this equals the total number of band members $ n $.\n\nSo we have:\n$$\nn = (r - 2)(m + 1)\n$$\n\nWe also have:\n$$\nn = rm + 2\n$$\n\nEquating the two expressions for $ n $:\n$$\nrm + 2 = (r - 2)(m + 1)\n$$\n\nExpanding the right-hand side:\n$$\nrm + 2 = rm + r - 2m - 2\n$$\n\nSimplify:\n$$\nrm + 2 = rm + r - 2m - 2\n$$\n\nSubtract $ rm $ from both sides:\n$$\n2 = r - 2m - 2\n$$\n\nSolve for $ r $:\n$$\nr = 2m + 4\n$$\n\nNow substitute $ r = 2m + 4 $ into the expression for $ n $:\n$$\nn = rm + 2 = (2m + 4)m + 2 = 2m^2 + 4m + 2\n$$\n\nWe are told $ n < 100 $, so:\n$$\n2m^2 + 4m + 2 < 100\n$$\n\nSolve the inequality:\n$$\n2m^2 + 4m + 2 < 100\n$$\n$$\n2m^2 + 4m < 98\n$$\n$$\nm^2 + 2m < 49\n$$\n\nTry integer values of $ m $ to find the largest possible $ n $ under 100.\n\nTry $ m = 6 $:\n$$\nn = 2(6)^2 + 4(6) + 2 = 2(36) + 24 + 2 = 72 + 24 + 2 = 98\n$$\n\nTry $ m = 7","cleanup_applied":"strip_think","finish_reason":"length"},"legacy_result":{"evaluator":"numeric_tolerance","passed":false,"score":0.0,"integration_outcome":"missing_final_marker"},"expected_result":{"semantic_outcome":"not_scored","semantic_score":null,"protocol_outcome":"noncompliant","integration_outcome":"unparseable"},"expected_change":"diagnostics_only","rationale":"The output was cut off before a final answer; the visible intermediate 98 must not be treated as an unambiguous submitted answer.","tags":["truncation","final_marker","cluster_runtime_output"]}
